# Pairs with AllocatorAboveOrphans. The issue #5799 defect: the post-failure
# resync re-seeds the allocator from the store alone (one past the highest
# stored entry), ignoring the abandoned calls still in motion, so it hands an
# offset out again beneath one of them.
MODULE: AllocatorAboveOrphansResyncRewindsToStoreTail
TARGET: AllocatorAboveOrphans
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the post-failure resync re-seeds from the store, beneath an abandoned call in motion
PERTURBS: Resync

--- FIND
    /\ resyncing = "resync"
    /\ inflight = {}
    /\ next' = ReseedNext
--- REPLACE
    /\ resyncing = "resync"
    /\ inflight = {}
\* MUTATION: re-seed from the store alone.
    /\ next' = RecoveredNext
--- END
